      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The majority holds that the Clean Air Act preempts Boulder's application of Colorado tort law to obtain damages for worldwide greenhouse-gas emissions because that liability interferes with the Act's allocation of emissions regulation to EPA and source States, applying the affected-state/source-state distinction drawn in Ouellette."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The holding is categorical for injured-state tort claims seeking compensation for aggregate interstate and international greenhouse-gas emissions, rather than immunity for fossil-fuel producers from all state tort law; it leaves ordinary deception claims not dependent on global emissions damages and source-state claims outside that categorical bar."
    }
